sues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.5.beta5.official.c81fd6c51\n- I know I saw this in other 4.5 betas, but I'm not sure which ones.  At least beta4.\n- Does not happen in 4.4.1\n\n### System information\n\nMacOS 15.6 (24G84)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf you create a simple standalone script that quits, the Godot icon remains in the MacOS dock until you click on it.  It then goes away.  The job appears to be gone, I cannot find it in the activity monitor or anywhere else.  It appears to just be an issue with the dock.\n\n```gdscript\nextends SceneTree\n\nfunc _init() -> void:\n\tprint(\"Hello World\")\n\tquit()\n```\n\nAwaiting for some amount of time seems to make it go away correctly.  For me, waiting .1 seconds was not enough, but .5 was.\n\n```gdscript\nextends SceneTree\n\nfunc _init() -> void:\n\tprint(\"Hello World\")\n\tawait create_timer(.5).timeout\n\tquit()\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRun this, check your dock for another Godot icon.  Click the icon, it goes away.\n```gdscript\nextends SceneTree\n\nfunc _init() -> void:\n\tprint(\"Hello World\")\n\tquit()\n```\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nSee steps to reproduce.","closed_by":{"login":"bitwes","id":1156520,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNTY1MjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1156520?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bitwes","html_url":"https://github.com/bitwes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bitwes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bitwes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bitwes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bitwes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bitwes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bitwes/or